<title>NEW ZEALAND: OECD sees NZ monetary conditions remaining firm.</title>
<headline>OECD sees NZ monetary conditions remaining firm.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Organisation for Economic Cooperation and Development, in a survey on New Zealand prepared before the formation of its new centre-right coalition government and released on Friday, said monetary conditions were likely to remain firm.</p>
<p>The Paris-based group representing 26 advanced economies also said there appeared to be significant downside risks to the growth outlook.</p>
</text>
